{
  "question": 5,
  "title": "Q5 Jordan form and matrix exponential",
  "subject": "Math",
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "q5-sol",
      "moduleId": "solution-steps",
      "title": "Worked solution",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 764,
      "anchorMode": "board-fixed-size",
      "solution": {
        "version": 1,
        "title": "Q5 · Jordan form and e^(At)",
        "problem": "$A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&1&1&-1\\\\-4&2&4&-3\\\\-1&1&3&-1\\\\-3&0&3&-1\\end{pmatrix}$. Find the Jordan form, and solve $x'=Ax$, $x(0)=(1,0,0,0)^T$.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s01",
            "math": "1+2+3+(-1) = 2+2+2+(-1)",
            "note": "Trace check: the eigenvalues 2, 2, 2, −1 sum to tr A = 5."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s02",
            "math": "(\\lambda-2)^3(\\lambda+1) = \\lambda^4-5\\lambda^3+6\\lambda^2+4\\lambda-8",
            "note": "Characteristic polynomial (λ − 2)³(λ + 1), expanded: the λ³ coefficient −5 = −tr A."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s03",
            "math": "J=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&0&0&0\\\\0&2&1&0\\\\0&0&2&1\\\\0&0&0&2\\end{pmatrix}",
            "note": "rank(A − 2I) = 3, rank(A − 2I)² = 2, rank(A − 2I)³ = 1: geometric multiplicity 4 − 3 = 1, so one 3×3 block J₃(2), plus J₁(−1)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s04",
            "math": "0+1+0-1 = 0,\\quad 0+2+0-3 = -1,\\quad 0+1+0-1 = 0,\\quad 0+0+0-1 = -1",
            "note": "Rows of A times w = (0, 1, 0, 1): Aw = (0, −1, 0, −1) = −w, so w is the λ = −1 eigenvector."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s05",
            "math": "1+0 = 1,\\quad -1+1 = 0,\\quad 0+0 = 0,\\quad -1+1 = 0",
            "note": "Split x₀ = u + w with u = (1, −1, 0, −1) in ker(A − 2I)³."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s06",
            "math": "-1-1+0+1 = -1,\\quad -4+0+0+3 = -1,\\quad -1-1+0+1 = -1,\\quad -3+0+0+3 = 0",
            "note": "Rows of N = A − 2I times u: Nu = (−1, −1, −1, 0)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s07",
            "math": "1-1-1+0 = -1,\\quad 4+0-4+0 = 0,\\quad 1-1-1+0 = -1,\\quad 3+0-3+0 = 0",
            "note": "N²u = N(Nu) = (−1, 0, −1, 0)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s08",
            "math": "1+0-1+0 = 0,\\quad 4+0-4+0 = 0,\\quad 1+0-1+0 = 0,\\quad 3+0-3+0 = 0",
            "note": "N³u = N(N²u) = 0, so the exponential series stops after t²/2."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s09",
            "math": "\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(\\left(1-t-\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}\\right) = \\left(1-t-\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}+\\left(e^{-t}-(1+t)e^{2t}\\right)+\\left(-\\left(t+\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}\\right)-\\left(e^{-t}-e^{2t}\\right)",
            "note": "x(t) = e^{2t}(u + tNu + t²N²u/2) + e^{−t}w. CAS check of row 1 of x′ = Ax."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s10",
            "math": "\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{-t}-(1+t)e^{2t}\\right) = -4\\left(1-t-\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}+2\\left(e^{-t}-(1+t)e^{2t}\\right)+4\\left(-\\left(t+\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}\\right)-3\\left(e^{-t}-e^{2t}\\right)",
            "note": "Row 2 of x′ = Ax."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s11",
            "math": "\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(-\\left(t+\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}\\right) = -\\left(1-t-\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}+\\left(e^{-t}-(1+t)e^{2t}\\right)+3\\left(-\\left(t+\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}\\right)-\\left(e^{-t}-e^{2t}\\right)",
            "note": "Row 3 of x′ = Ax."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s12",
            "math": "\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{-t}-e^{2t}\\right) = -3\\left(1-t-\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}+3\\left(-\\left(t+\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right)e^{2t}\\right)-\\left(e^{-t}-e^{2t}\\right)",
            "note": "Row 4 of x′ = Ax."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s13",
            "math": "(1-0-0)e^{0} = 1,\\quad e^{0}-(1+0)e^{0} = 0,\\quad -(0+0)e^{0} = 0,\\quad e^{0}-e^{0} = 0",
            "note": "Initial condition: x(0) = (1, 0, 0, 0)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s14",
            "math": "\\left(1-1-\\frac12\\right)e^{2} = -\\frac{e^2}{2} \\approx -3.6945",
            "note": "x₁(1)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s15",
            "math": "e^{-1}-2e^{2} \\approx -14.4102",
            "note": "x₂(1)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s16",
            "math": "-\\left(1+\\frac12\\right)e^{2} = -\\frac{3e^2}{2} \\approx -11.0836",
            "note": "x₃(1)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q5-sol-s17",
            "math": "e^{-1}-e^{2} \\approx -7.0212",
            "note": "x₄(1)."
          }
        ],
        "answer": "J=J_3(2)\\oplus J_1(-1);\\quad x(1)=\\left(-\\tfrac{e^2}{2},\\ e^{-1}-2e^2,\\ -\\tfrac{3e^2}{2},\\ e^{-1}-e^2\\right)\\approx(-3.6945,-14.4102,-11.0836,-7.0212)",
        "source": {
          "kind": "manual"
        }
      }
    },
